    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **47 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` feature on `POST /api/owners`, following the existing Spring/MapStruct conventions in the codebase.\n\n**What the change does:** when a request includes an ISO `birthDate`, the owner is stored with it and the response (and later `GET /api/owners/{id}`) exposes an `ageBand` derived against the owner's `registrationDate`: `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+). When no `birthDate` is supplied, `ageBand` is absent.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (input, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema and read-only `ageBand` (string) to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time.\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field (`birth_date` column) with getter/setter.\n3. **`util/AgeBands.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper computing the band via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()`, mirroring the style of `Memberships`/`Localities`. Returns `null` when either date is absent.\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `ageBand` mapping expression calling `AgeBands.ageBand(...)`, alongside the other derived fields. MapStruct already maps `birthDate` from the fields DTO onto the entity by name.\n5. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column so the value persists and survives the `GET` readback.\n\nI kept `ageBand` a plain string rather than an OpenAPI enum, matching how `locality`/`contactPreference` are done and keeping the mapper expression a simple `String`.\n\nThe acceptance test `Cp34Tests` (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, and all 47 tests remain green.",
